DOCUMENT();        # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros(
"PG.pl",
"PGbasicmacros.pl",
"PGchoicemacros.pl",
"PGanswermacros.pl",
"PGgraphmacros.pl",
"PGmatrixmacros.pl", 
"PGnumericalmacros.pl",
"PGauxiliaryFunctions.pl"
);

TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 1;

$a = random(-9,-1,1);
$b = random(2,9,1);

$ans1 = $b - $a;
$ans2 = ($b**2 - $a**2)/2;
$ans3 = ($b**3 - $a**3)/3;
$ans4 = ($b**4 - $a**4)/4;

BEGIN_TEXT

Let \(T\colon P_3 \to \mathbb{R}\) be the linear transformation defined by \[T(f(x)) = \int_{$a}^{$b} f(x) dx.\]
Let \( B = \lbrace 1,x,x^2,x^3\rbrace \) be the standard basis of \(P_3\).$BR
Let \( B' \) be the standard basis of \(\mathbb{R}\).
$PAR
Then the matrix \([T]_{B'B}\) of \(T\) with respect to these two bases is
$BR
\{ answer_matrix(1,4,15) \} 

END_TEXT

ANS(num_cmp($ans1));
ANS(num_cmp($ans2));
ANS(num_cmp($ans3));
ANS(num_cmp($ans4));

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.

